<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suniti Devi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1864–1932</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suniti Devi was Maharani of Cooch Behar, the daughter of the reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keshab-chandra-sen">Keshab Chandra Sen</a> and wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nripendra-narayan">Nripendra Narayan</a>, whom she married in 1878. Her marriage, contrary to her father's campaign against child marriage, divided the Brahmo Samaj. She worked for women's education, founding a girls' school in Cooch Behar.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suniti-devi.jpg" alt="Suniti Devi" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: London Stereoscopic Company (original); colorized by Regalhist5 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maharani_Suniti_Devi_of_Cooch_Behar_(%E0%A6%B8%E0%A7%81%E0%A6%A8%E0%A7%80%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%BF_%E0%A6%A6%E0%A7%87%E0%A6%AC%E0%A7%80),_c._1885_%E2%80%93_Colorized.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
